WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.900
(soft music)

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:03.670
- [Narrator] Seaweed
is a common ingredient

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.060
in Japanese cuisine.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.213
But, there's unique type
growing in the Pacific Ocean.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:24.827
(upbeat music)

00:00:24.827 --> 00:00:27.230
- [Narrator] Seventy miles off
the coast of mainland Japan

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:29.420
is the small island of Okinawa.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:32.150
Home to one of the most
unusual farming methods

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:32.983
in the world.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:41.050
- [Narrator] Mr. Oshiro comes
from a seafaring family.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:44.000
And today, he's one of the
farmers growing mozuku,

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.763
a special seaweed only
grown in these waters.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.210
- [Narrator] Each fall,
a web of nets are laced

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:59.250
with mozuku seedlings on land.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:02.800
Then, Mr. Oshiro and his
son lay the nets in rows

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:03.873
in the shallow water.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:08.200
This ingenious system allows
the mozuku to grow sustainably

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.530
by not creating additional waste.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:13.060
And when the time is
right, it is harvested

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:15.633
with two boats and their giant vacuum.

00:01:18.499 --> 00:01:21.166
(engine starts)

00:01:38.756 --> 00:01:41.080
- [Narrator] The day’s harvest
is then taken to his factory

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.780
where it's cleaned, weighed and processed.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:45.340
Then, it's off to the markets

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.143
to sell his underwater treasure.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.000
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.580
- [Narrator] Mozuku is in high demand.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.990
It's packed with nutrients,
so many people eat it

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:58.130
for a health boost.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:01:59.780
But, that wasn't always the case.

00:02:24.486 --> 00:02:26.986
(piano music)

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:29.110
- [Narrator] In recent years,

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:32.120
Mr. Oshiro has seen a change in the ocean.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:34.823
So the future of his mozuku is uncertain.

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:20.760
- [Narrator] Despite the challenges,

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.210
Mr. Oshiro's dedication proves this work

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:25.160
is more than just a day job.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:28.290
For him, it's about
maintaining a family tradition

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.793
and passing on his father's
respect for the sea.

